 you had  with your kids when you told him that  there was no tournament  it was difficult you know we we uh we're  in brooklyn  for our tournament for the a-10  tournament and and uh we were scheduled  to play the winner of vcu  uh in umass and uh i was headed to to  watch that game  when the news came out that our  tournament was canceled so  i had to to quickly get the team  together back in our hotel and break the  news to them and  it was difficult especially when you had  to look in the eyes of you know trey  landers and ryan mike's of our two  seniors  knowing that you know this was this was  their last opportunity to  to compete for an 8-10 tournament  championship and what that meant  and you know we we also realized that  the dominoes could fall and  impact the the ncaa tournament so we  were hopeful that  maybe that there would be a postponement  rather than a cancellation  and then once we once we got on the  plane to head  back to dayton later that afternoon the  word came out  uh that the ncaa tournament had been  canceled so  it was kind of a you know surreal moment  it was  very quiet playing right back and trying  to gather my thoughts and met with the  team after and  a lot of emotion you know because they  realized that was it you know that they  wouldn't get a chance to play with each  other anymore and  you know that's difficult when it's not  in your control you know you can  you can probably deal with you know a  loss  had you had a chance to go out there and  compete and on a given night a team had  been  just better than you on that given night  uh but to not get a chance to compete  and have it in that way uh you know that  that's really difficult but  we got a group of guys that you know  they they uh  they really supported each other all  year and continue to support each other  i think as we kind of  go through what the rest of the country  is dealing with  and when we're all dealing with uh you  know with the uh the covet 19  that's uh 