 a wait-and-see approach to what  kevin's decision was going to be and i  think everybody in the building  respected the fact that he'd earned that  right to make a decision about what he  felt was best  for his future so once he made that  decision  you know we uh uh just kind of put our  trust in  in the front office to to move forward  and i i think they did a great job with  that and obviously the following year  uh russell westbrook became the mvp of  the league and you know  made history himself and and so uh you  know my two years there were a great  experience and  got a chance to be around some some  extremely talented and  and uh just just really great people  from  players to coaches and uh the management  team uh it was it was a great experience  who was easier to coach durant or  westbrook  well they're both great players you know  so so i  i think you you know you talk about  their their uh  their talents and their just their their  ability to  make everybody around them better you  know i i i enjoyed  you know being around both of them  handicapped ob  topping do you think is there a better  player in college basketball than ob  yeah i mean i i don't again you know i  haven't seen everybody there's a lot of  really great  great players out there but i think no  one can take away  what obi did from the start to the  finish you know for our team  we felt like you know we had a chance to  be  to be special when the season started  but i think when you look at  you know we were we were picked to  finish third in our conference and  nobody had us you know one of those  teams that were being talked about as  one of the top  30 40 teams in the country you know and  uh  obviously what obi did but what the rest  of our guys did over the course of the  season  just in terms of their buy-in their  willingness to support each other  sacrifice for each other  and uh you know hobie really separated  himself from  the beginning of the season all the way  through and